pan class="enc-snip">Gümüştekin Gazi was the Danishmendid emir from about 1104 to 1134, son of Danishmend Gazi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guna-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guna-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Guna people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Guna, formerly spelled Kuna, are an indigenous people of Panama and north-western Colombia, living mainly on the San Blas islands and the Caribbean coast of Darién.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/guna-yala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guna-yala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Guna Yala</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Guna Yala, formerly San Blas, is an indigenous territory (comarca) of the Guna people along Panama's north-eastern Caribbean coast, including some 365 islands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/gunabhadra"><span class="enc-name">Gunabhadra</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gunabhadra was a Digambara Jain monk and author of the ninth century, a disciple of Jinasena, working in the Rashtrakuta empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gunakamadeva"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gunakamadeva.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gunakamadeva</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gunakamadeva was a king of the Kathmandu Valley in the Thakuri period, traditionally placed in the 10th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gundahar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gundahar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gundahar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gundahar was a king of the Burgundians in the early 5th century who, as a Roman ally, set up a Burgundian kingdom on the Rhine around 411, traditionally centred on Worms.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gunderic"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gunderic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gunderic</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gunderic was king of the Hasding Vandals from about 407 to 428.</span></a></li></ul>
